{"orgCode":"4700","name":"Department of Community Services and Development","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"The mission of the Department of Community Services and Development is to improve the economic security of vulnerable Californians by partnering with nonprofit and local government organizations dedicated to helping low-income individuals and families achieve and maintain economic security, pay their energy bills, and make their homes more energy efficient.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":330286,"cy":412783,"by":344679},"positions":{"py":122.3,"cy":124.9,"by":124.9},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":12765,"cy":10957,"by":11050}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/4700","kind":"department","name":"Department of Community Services and Development","code":"4700","amounts":{"py":330286,"cy":412783,"by":344679},"positions":{"py":122.3,"cy":124.9,"by":124.9},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1129,"cy":452,"by":0},"special":{"py":155,"cy":2897,"by":0},"bond":{"py":0,"cy":230,"by":230},"federal":{"py":329002,"cy":409204,"by":344449}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181","kind":"program","name":"Energy Programs","code":"4181","amounts":{"py":261150,"cy":341151,"by":272989},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1028,"cy":452,"by":0},"special":{"py":155,"cy":2897,"by":0},"bond":{"py":0,"cy":230,"by":230},"federal":{"py":259967,"cy":337572,"by":272759}},"positions":{"py":89.3,"cy":93.2,"by":93.2},"description":"4181 - The Energy Programs assist low-income households in meeting their immediate and long-term home energy needs through financial assistance, energy conservation, weatherization, and renewable energy services.\n\nThe Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program (LIHEAP) provides financial assistance to eligible low-income households to offset the costs of heating and/or cooling residential dwellings, assistance for weather-related or energy-related emergencies, and weatherization services to improve the energy efficiency of low-income residential dwellings and safeguard the health and safety of household occupants.\n\nThe Department of Energy Weatherization Assistance Program provides weatherization to improve the energy efficiency of low-income residential dwellings and safeguard the health and safety of household occupants.\n\nThe Low-Income Weatherization Program (LIWP) provides energy efficiency and renewable energy services in low-income single-family farmworker and multi-family dwellings to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and lower energy costs. LIWP projects include energy efficient weatherization and solar photovoltaic system installations.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":20638,"cy":25789,"by":22457},"Local Assistance":{"py":240512,"cy":315582,"by":250582}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1028,"cy":452,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1028,"cy":452,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1028,"cy":452,"by":0}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":259967,"cy":337572,"by":272759},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":259967,"cy":337572,"by":272759}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":19455,"cy":21990,"by":22177},"Local Assistance":{"py":240512,"cy":315582,"by":250582}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f3228","kind":"fund","name":"Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund","code":"3228","amounts":{"py":118,"cy":2897,"by":0},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":118,"cy":2897,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":118,"cy":2897,"by":0}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f3398","kind":"fund","name":"California Emergency Relief Fund","code":"3398","amounts":{"py":37,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":37,"cy":0,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":37,"cy":0,"by":0}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f6093","kind":"fund","name":"Safe Drinking Water, Wildfire Prevention, Drought Preparedness, and Clean Air Fund","code":"6093","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":230,"by":230},"byFundType":{"bond":{"py":0,"cy":230,"by":230}},"extra":{"fundType":"bond","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":230,"by":230}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4181/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":220,"by":50},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":220,"by":50}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":220,"by":50}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":220,"by":50}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4700/4185","kind":"program","name":"Community Services","code":"4185","amounts":{"py":69136,"cy":71632,"by":71690},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":101,"cy":0,"by":0},"federal":{"py":69035,"cy":71632,"by":71690}},"positions":{"py":33,"cy":31.7,"by":31.7},"description":"4185 - COMMUNITY SERVICES\n\nThe Community Services Block Grant (CSBG) is designed to enable local government and nonprofit community organizations to help low-income families achieve and maintain economic security through a broad range of services and activities. These include education, employment services, emergency services, housing, income support and management, and health and nutritional services, among others.\n\nThe California Earned Income Tax Credit (CalEITC) benefits low-income, working Californians by providing cash-back tax credits to boost the income of eligible individuals and families. Since 2016-17, the Department has worked with the Franchise Tax Board to provide grant opportunities for community-based organizations to increase awareness of CalEITC and free tax preparation assistance programs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4968,"cy":7105,"by":7426},"Local Assistance":{"py":76933,"cy":75264,"by":75264}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children